  #line-at(93.72pt, 354.959pt, "Abstract: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.33pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(138.179pt, 354.959pt, "This article presents a novel fabrication route for miniaturized piezoelectric actuators that ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 366.899pt, "relies exclusively on processes based on femtosecond (fs) laser ablation. Previous work has already ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 378.779pt, "demonstrated that fs-lasers are uniquely suited for the fabrication of piezoelectric actuators based on ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 390.659pt, "PMN-PT, which are required for multiaxial strain-tuning of quantum dots (QDs) to enable, e.g. the ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 402.539pt, "generation of highly entangled photon pairs. Building on these foundations, the present work ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 414.478pt, "advances actuator performance and capabilities by introducing a local thinning strategy. This ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 426.358pt, "approach allows the realization of smaller devices, which in turn enables lower operating voltages, ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 438.298pt, "while simultaneously offering the possibility of integrating multiple quantum light sources on a single ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 450.118pt, "chip. The article provides a detailed description of the full fabrication chain, entirely based on fs-laser ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 462.058pt, "processing steps, from substrate thinning to metal layer structuring and final device definition. A ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 473.938pt, "particular focus is placed on the final cutting process, where the implementation of a third-harmonic ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 485.877pt, "ultraviolet (UV) fs-laser wavelength significantly improves edge quality and shape definition ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 497.757pt, "compared to the second harmonic (SH) wavelength used in previous work. The device fabricated ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 509.697pt, "through the combination of local thinning and UV-based cutting promises not only to enhance the ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 521.517pt, "efficiency of strain transfer but also to ensure the mechanical stability required for practical ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 533.457pt, "applications. ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 552.896pt, "These results establish fs-laser-based fabrication as a versatile and scalable method for next-")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 564.776pt, "generation piezoelectric actuators, paving the way for advanced strain-engineering approaches in ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 576.716pt, "semiconductor quantum optics and integrated quantum photonics. ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 596.095pt, "Keywords: femtosecond laser, piezo actuator, laser micro structuring, laser ablation, PMN-PT, strain-")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 608.035pt, "tuning, quantum dot ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.072pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.72pt, 651.24pt, "1. Introduction")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.33pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.721pt, 664.2pt, "Piezoelectric materials play a crucial role in Micro-Electro-Mechanical Systems (MEMS) due to their ")
  #line-at(93.721pt, 676.08pt, "unique ability to convert mechanical into electrical energy and vice versa. This property makes them ")
  #line-at(93.722pt, 687.96pt, "particularly suitable for applications in sensors and actuators. Notable advantages of these materials ")
  #line-at(93.722pt, 699.84pt, "include a large dynamic range, low power consumption, and minimal hysteresis values [1]. Among ")
  #line-at(93.722pt, 711.78pt, "the various piezoelectric materials, lead magnesium niobate-lead titanate (PMN-PT) in single crystal ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.33pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.72pt, 77.4pt, "form stands out due to its exceptionally high piezoelectric constant (d33) and coupling factors, as well ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 89.28pt, "as its high sensitivity. These characteristics facilitate its use in high-quality sensors and actuators [2] ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 101.22pt, "[3] [4]. ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 120.659pt, "In addition to their applications in MEMS, PMN-PT materials are also utilized in ultrasound ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 132.479pt, "technology, where high sensitivity and a wide bandwidth are essential for producing recognizable ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 144.419pt, "imaging [5] [6] [7]. Notably, PMN-PT materials maintain their effective performance even at ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 156.299pt, "cryogenic temperatures, making them suitable for applications in low-temperature environments [8]. ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 175.738pt, "The precise controllability and high piezoelectric response of PMN-PT makes it an ideal material for ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 187.618pt, "the realization of actuators for strain-tuning of quantum dot emitters. Strain influences the band ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 199.558pt, "structure and optical properties of semiconductors. The ability to introduce deliberate in-plane strain ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 211.438pt, "fields in semiconductor quantum dots opens exciting possibilities such as the production of ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 223.318pt, "polarization entangled photons via tuning of the fine structure splitting in the biexciton-exciton decay ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 235.197pt, "[9]. However, this application requires a complex multi-axis actuator which can be operated at ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 247.137pt, "cryogenic temperatures.[10], [11], [12], [13]. ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 266.577pt, "As actuators based on single crystal PMN-PT are particularly delicate due to their brittleness, small ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 278.456pt, "dimensions and thin substrates, processing options are very limited. Moreover, special processing ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 290.396pt, "methods are required to bring the PMN-PT substrate into the appropriate shape, as required for multi-")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 302.276pt, "axial strain tuning. Properties such as a resolution in the micrometer range, arbitrary geometries, low ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 314.156pt, "surface roughness and sharp edges must be fulfilled in order to achieve repeatability, reliability of the ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 326.036pt, "function, as well as yield.  ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 345.475pt, "Various processing techniques have been employed for structuring and cutting PMN-PT substrates. ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 357.355pt, "These are wet etching [14], dry etching [15] [5], reactive ion etching [16] or ion milling [3], [17].  ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 369.295pt, "Each process has its advantages, but also limitations such as long processing times, limited geometric ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 381.175pt, "possibilities or insufficient processing quality. Laser ablation in general offers a flexible direct writing ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 393.115pt, "process with good process times and the potential for high quality devices [15], [18], [19], [20].  ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 412.554pt, "In our previous work on the processing of PMN-PT and applications of the actuators in the field of ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 424.434pt, "semiconductor-based quantum optics, we were able to demonstrate the high potential of femtosecond ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 436.314pt, "laser processing [21]. Actuators of various geometries were realized by laser cutting with the second ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 448.194pt, "harmonic of the femtosecond laser at 523 nm. In addition, the individual electrical contacts were ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 460.133pt, "patterned by selective ablation of a gold layer using the same laser source. In this way, devices with a ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 472.013pt, "total thickness of 300 µm and a side length of 5 mm were developed. The minimum distance between ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 483.953pt, "the individual actuator arms was limited to 30 µm due to the laser parameters and the sample ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 495.833pt, "thickness. ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 515.272pt, "Current research efforts in the field of quantum emitters focus on higher integration density, which ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 527.152pt, "leads to a need for miniaturized actuators. To ensure comparable strain-transfer properties, our new ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 539.032pt, "design strategy incorporates localized thinning of the active regions, as illustrated in Fig. 1. This ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 550.972pt, "approach offers the advantage of achieving higher electric fields at the same applied voltage while ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 562.852pt, "maintaining mechanical stability via the thicker surrounding areas. Additionally, laser cutting within ")
  #line-at(93.719pt, 574.792pt, "these thinned regions enables the realisation of narrower cutting widths and potentially higher strain ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 586.671pt, "amplification. However, this new generation of actuators leads to a more complex manufacturing ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 598.551pt, "workflow compared to the previously published strain-tuning platforms. For the final device, it is ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 610.431pt, "critical that the fabrication produces clean, defect-free surfaces – without debris, cracks, or fracture ")
  #line-at(93.72pt, 622.371pt, "points – as these affect its functionality during use.  ")
]

