  #line-at(474.899pt, 144.421pt, " After a ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 156.361pt, "cleaning step, a coating of 10 nm titanium and 150 nm gold was applied. After that, a rectangular ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 168.241pt, "structuring path was ablated using the femtosecond laser, with one of the long sides placed centrally ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 180.181pt, "over the cavity (see schematic of Fig. 8). After structuring, the electrical separation between the inner ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 192.001pt, "and outer surfaces of the rectangle was tested both on the cavity floor and on the substrate surface. In ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 203.941pt, "addition, the conductivity from the bottom to the top surface was also measured as in the coating tests. ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 223.321pt, "One characteristic of ablation with ultrashort laser pulses is a sharply defined ablation threshold. This ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 235.261pt, "was measured using Liu's method [23] and is 0.14 J/cm² in the case of gold and 0.45 J/cm² for PMN-")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 247.141pt, "PT for a pulse duration of 350 fs at a wavelength of 523 nm. These values show the potential for ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 259.081pt, "selective structuring of gold on PMN-PT, which we demonstrate below.  ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 278.462pt, "For the layer structuring, a repetition rate of 100 kHz and a processing speed of 700 mm/s were ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 290.402pt, "selected. Different samples were structured with power values of 0.882 W and 0.788 W, all with 2 and ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 302.282pt, "3 pattern repetitions. The focus was positioned to half the depth of the cavity. This provides the ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 314.162pt, "highest possible value for the intensity at the side edge. This is advantageous as the fluence value is ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 326.042pt, "smaller compared to flat surfaces due to projection onto an inclined plane. The Rayleigh length of the ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 337.982pt, "focused beam is 696 µm and is considerably higher than the depth of the structure.  ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 357.422pt, "Electrical resistance between separated areas on the floor, as well as on the substrate surface, should ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 369.302pt, "be very high. Measurements show that each combination of power values and repetitions (8 in total) ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 381.242pt, "results in a resistance value exceeding the maximum possible measurement value of 50 MOhm for the ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 393.122pt, "multimeter used. In addition, the resistance of the gold layer over the side edge, as carried out in the ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 405.062pt, "coating tests, was also examined which resulted in values between 3 and 9 Ω for all samples. The ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 416.882pt, "SEM image in Fig. 8 shows the result of the structuring process at a laser power of 0.882 W and a ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 428.822pt, "repetition number of three. The slight difference in the shade of grey inside and outside the rectangle, ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 440.702pt, "which is due to different electrical charges, already visualises the distinct electrical properties of these ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 452.642pt, "areas. The measuring points for conductivity are also shown schematically. ")
