// arXiv source page 10
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-10.png", width: 343pt), 135.5pt, 407pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.32pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 77.4pt, "operated at a wavelength of 523 nm. However, if the actuator design is subjected to a further ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 89.34pt, "reduction in size as it is in this work, these process parameters are no longer applicable and need to be ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 101.16pt, "adjusted to achieve the precision requirements. For this reason, a new approach is chosen in this ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 113.1pt, "study.  ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 132.541pt, "As a first change in the parameter set, the wavelength of the laser was reduced to the third harmonic at ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 144.421pt, "348 nm. This provides the advantage of a smaller spot radius on the one hand and improved ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 156.361pt, "absorption conditions on the other. Data from the literature determine the band gap of monocrystalline ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 168.241pt, "PMN-PT with a value in the range of 3.1 to 3.3 eV, depending on material composition and ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 180.181pt, "temperature [31]. This is just between the photon energy of the laser at its second (2.37 eV) and third ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 192.001pt, "harmonic (3.56 eV), respectively. For this reason, the energy can be deposited by linear absorption ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 203.941pt, "using the UV wavelength in contrast to the previously used cutting process, where one had to rely on ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 215.821pt, "a two-photon absorption mechanism. This has the advantages of an intensity-independent deposition ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 227.761pt, "of energy within the optical penetration depth and, as a consequence, of a reduced effect to the ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 239.641pt, "adjacent bulk material. ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 259.081pt, "As already mentioned, the refined actuator concepts are based on a locally thinned area in which a ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 270.961pt, "miniaturised design is realised using the UV fs-laser. However, as PMN-PT is difficult to manipulate ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 282.901pt, "mechanically at this greatly reduced thickness of 100 µm, a substrate with a thickness of 300 µm was ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 294.721pt, "used for the first tests to evaluate the cutting edge. To refine the process parameters and evaluate the ")
  #line-at(93.778pt, 306.661pt, "laser exit edge, the substrates were thinned to the reduced thickness of 100 µm using laser thinning as ")
  #line-at(93.778pt, 318.542pt, "described in section 3.1.  ")
  #line-at(93.778pt, 337.982pt, "The SEM images in Fig. 9 show the design of a three-unit actuator, realised with different power ")
  #line-at(93.778pt, 349.862pt, "values and variable number of passes. Two sets of equidistant lines were applied alternately to ")
  #line-at(93.778pt, 361.802pt, "achieve the required cutting depth. First, 10 lines were applied with a distance of 4.5 µm to ensure ")
  #line-at(93.777pt, 373.682pt, "removal even at the wider parts of the geometry, so that there were no free-standing parts at the end of ")
  #line-at(93.777pt, 385.562pt, "the cutting process. Then, additional equidistant lines with reduced distance (5 x 2 µm) should lead to ")
  #line-at(93.777pt, 397.502pt, "a more distinctive cutting edge.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.459pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(100.08pt, 685.5pt, "Fig. 9")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.459pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(120.36pt, 685.5pt, " SEM images of a three-leg actuator design cut with different laser and process parameters using the third harmonic ")
  #line-at(99.18pt, 695.22pt, "wavelength. For the process, two sets of equidistant lines were applied; 5 lines with a distance of 2 µm and 10 lines with a ")
  #line-at(106.5pt, 705pt, "distance of 4.5 µm. In the upper row results for three different values of laser power and a repetition number of 100 is ")
  #line-at(142.74pt, 714.72pt, "shown. Row 2 and 3 show results after 200 repetition and an additional cutting design overview.  ")
]

// arXiv source page 11
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-11.png", width: 337.5pt), 137pt, 426pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.32pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 77.4pt, "The laser was operated at a repetition rate of 250 kHz. The scanner speed was 1250 mm/s for all tests. ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 89.34pt, "The results shown in the upper row were obtained with a repetition of the cutting line pattern of 100. ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 101.16pt, "It can be clearly seen that the ablation depth is very low, especially at a power of 0.4 W. The ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 113.1pt, "arrangement of the cutting lines creates a cushion-shaped base inside the cutting geometry. This leads ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 124.98pt, "to a very clear depression along the actual cutting line. If the laser power is increased, the ablated ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 136.92pt, "depth is considerably higher, although the quality of the edges hardly shows any change. At a ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 148.8pt, "repetition of 200, the base area can only be seen at the lowest power of 0.4 W. The further course of ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 160.74pt, "the edge can no longer be evaluated. Evaluating the cutting edge on the laser entrance side shows a ")
  #line-at(93.779pt, 172.62pt, "high quality with no evidence of any breakouts for the power value of 1.1 W. Since there is slight ")
  #line-at(93.778pt, 184.5pt, "melting recognized at 2 W, the following tests will be performed with the power value of 1.1 W.  ")
  #line-at(93.778pt, 203.941pt, "To estimate the quality to be expected on the exit side, the bottom of the cavity for a power of 1.1W at ")
  #line-at(93.778pt, 215.821pt, "100 repetitions can be evaluated. This already shows increasing irregularities with depth, which ")
  #line-at(93.777pt, 227.761pt, "suggest that an adaptation of the machining strategy is required to improve the quality.  ")
  #line-at(93.777pt, 247.141pt, "In this alternative approach, instead of performing cuts using equidistant lines, the actuator geometry ")
  #line-at(93.777pt, 259.081pt, "is processed using a line hatch pattern with the process parameters as described in section 3.1. This ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 270.961pt, "allows a pre-thinning of the geometry with the highest surface quality and a flat inner area. SEM ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 282.901pt, "images in Fig. 10 show the actuator geometry during thinning for different values of pattern ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 294.721pt, "repetition. Due to the small dimensions and the Gaussian beam profile, a rounded mold is formed. ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 306.661pt, "Starting from a repetition of 15, slight waviness appears at the bottom of the structure. Above a ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 318.541pt, "repetition of 70, an irregular side edge forms at the bottom of the structure. ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 337.982pt, "As a lower fluence is used when thinning compared to cutting, a cavity with a lower side edge angle is ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 349.862pt, "created. As already discussed in [21], the angle of the side edge depends solely on the ratio of the ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 361.802pt, "laser fluence to the ablation threshold of the material. It is expected that the higher fluence during ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 373.682pt, "cutting will widen the cavity, which should have a positive effect on the cut edge definition. ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 393.122pt, " After a defined number of repetitions, the cutting procedure switches to the actual cutting process ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 405.062pt, "with a set of equidistant lines and higher fluence values. This is intended to improve the quality of the ")
  #line-at(93.776pt, 416.942pt, "final cutting edge on the laser entrance as well as on the laser exit side. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.459pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 652.38pt, "Fig. 10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.459pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.26pt, 652.38pt, " SEM images of cavities generated by a line hatch pattern for an increasing number of pattern repetitions. As the ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 662.16pt, "number of repetitions increases, a rounded mould first forms, which deepens more and more and develops into a cut edge for ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 671.88pt, "repetitions higher than 40. A trough formation in the ablation is already recognisable from the 5th repetition, which ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 681.54pt, "transforms into a trench from the 15th repetition. The lateral flanks become increasingly steep and misshapen. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.32pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 702.48pt, "In preparation for the final cutting tests, circular cavities with a residual thickness of 100 µm were ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 714.36pt, "created. A geometrically split actuator, each side with two electrically controllable arms, is realised in ")
]

// arXiv source page 12
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-12.png", width: 380pt), 93.5pt, 122pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.32pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 77.4pt, "these cavities. In preparation for the process, the substrate is bonded to a ceramic sample holder using ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 89.34pt, "polyvinyl alcohol (PVA). Care is taken to ensure that both the front and the back side of the piezo ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 101.16pt, "substrate are fully covered with the coating.  This is necessary in order to be able to remove deposits ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 113.1pt, "from the cutting process together with the PVA layers. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.459pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 288.3pt, "Fig. 11")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.459pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.26pt, 288.3pt, " SEM images of a UV-laser cut actuator, processed within a laser-thinned area with residual sample thickness of 100 ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 298.08pt, "µm. The smallest inter-arm distance on the laser exit side is with a value of just 5 µm a significant reduction compared to ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 307.8pt, "actual designs realised with the SH wavelength. This has a direct effect on the achievable strain values with this new ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 317.52pt, "approach. Additionally, the lack of any irregularities on the back side of the actuator is crucial for subsequent bonding of the ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 327.24pt, "quantum emitter devices on this strain tuning platform. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.32pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 348.12pt, "Fig. 11 shows the front and back side of the final cut actuator after the protective coating has been ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 360.06pt, "removed. Deposit residues can still be seen inside the cavity which can be explained by insufficient ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 371.94pt, "coverage with PVA. ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 391.38pt, "Looking at the cut, a sharp, well-defined edge can be seen on both the laser entrance and the exit side. ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 403.26pt, "The exit side in particular is very critical for subsequent processes, as this is where the semiconductor ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 415.2pt, "membrane containing the quantum emitters is to be bonded. The SEM image on the right does not ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 427.08pt, "show any elevations or breakouts at the edges of the cut regions. This is a decisive improvement ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 438.961pt, "compared to the results with the second harmonic wavelength. If one compares the cut width at the ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 450.9pt, "exit side with 5 µm at the smallest point in comparison to 10-15 µm achieved with SH, a significant ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 462.781pt, "reduction is also possible through the use of UV. We expect this reduced width to enable higher strain ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 474.721pt, "values with reduced operating voltage compared to previously used tuning platforms. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.237pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 515.28pt, "5. Conclusion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.32pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 527.58pt, "In this work, we successfully demonstrated the fabrication of miniaturized and structurally complex ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 539.52pt, "piezo actuators based on single crystal PMN-PT using exclusively ultrashort pulsed laser processing ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 551.4pt, "for local sample thinning, electrode structuring and actuator cutting. In particular, the use of UV ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 563.34pt, "wavelengths enabled highly precise laser cutting, which proved essential for achieving the required ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 575.22pt, "resolution and structural precision. The newly developed process sequence enables actuator designs ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 587.1pt, "that offer promising new approaches for applications in the field of multiaxial strain-tuning, such as ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 598.98pt, "the integration of multiple individually addressed quantum emitters or the realisation of higher and ")
  #line-at(93.78pt, 610.92pt, "more directional strain values with miniaturized devices.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.237pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 651.48pt, "Acknowledgements ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.32pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(93.78pt, 663.78pt, "Parts of the work was funded within the QuantERA Programme that has received funding from the ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 675.72pt, "EU H2020 research and innovation programme under GA No 101017733 via the project QD-E-QKD ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 687.6pt, "and from the MUR (Ministero dell’Università e della Ricerca) through the PNRR MUR Project ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 699.54pt, "PE0000023-NQSTI and via the Project MEEDGARD: grant.13948955, EPSRC EP/Z000556/1  and ")
  #line-at(93.781pt, 711.42pt, "425333704 FWF-DFG. ")
]

